# Known DICOM viewing limitations

## Interactive viewer

The viewer preserves access to the originals for these objects, which lack
a dedicated preview:

- Philips private CT transfer syntax
- Philips HP Live 3D 02
- Raw Data Storage
- RT Structure Set Storage
- Enhanced US Volume Storage

Grayscale presentation states can apply supported windows, crop, orientation
and annotations. Sampled Presentation LUTs in a presentation state remain
unsupported. The viewer supports sampled grayscale Modality, VOI and
Presentation LUTs stored in images, including in existing archives.

Surface Segmentation previews need WebGL. Facets with more than three points
are unsupported. See [supported formats](docs/GUIDE.md#image-support).

## Display differences

| Object or display condition | PDF reference image | Interactive viewer |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Sampled grayscale LUTs stored in an image | Diagnostic page | Supported Modality, VOI and Presentation LUTs applied |
| Grayscale `SIGMOID` window | Diagnostic page | Supported |
| Native or RLE unsigned 16-bit RGB | Diagnostic page | Supported |
| Private GE 3D layout | Diagnostic page | Depends on the stored encoding and pixel layout |
| HTJ2K | Diagnostic page | Supported codestreams and layouts |
| Parametric Map | Diagnostic page | Supported integer and native floating-point maps |
| Surface Segmentation | Diagnostic page | WebGL mesh preview for supported facets |
| Retired JPEG spectral selection and progressive transfer syntaxes | Depends on the Java provider | Outside current viewer support |
| Video or waveform objects | Diagnostic page | Use a viewer for the object type |

The PDF renderer limits each frame to 16,777,216 pixels. The interactive viewer
limits frames to 33,554,432 pixels and also checks canvas dimensions and available
memory. A supported top-level grayscale LINEAR window with center and width both
zero uses an automatic window for PDF reference pages and interactive display.
Deflated grayscale images can use the same padding-aware automatic window as
native images. The [format matrix](docs/GUIDE.md#image-support) lists encodings,
and the [synthetic fixtures](fixtures/README.md) describe tested cases.

## Input errors and recovery

Invalid pixel bit layouts, inconsistent RT Dose frame counts, missing required
file-meta information and truncated data can prevent display. Check the selected
file's metadata and any diagnostic PDF page for details.

Choose **Save → Original file**, or use the download button next to the entry
under **Metadata → Other supplied files**. The CLI also supports `extract`.
See the [format matrix](docs/GUIDE.md#image-support) and
[recovery instructions](docs/GUIDE.md#save-original-files).
